## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js portfolio project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package**
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 1.3.1 to dependencies using pnpm
- Package manager: pnpm (version 10.28.0)

**2. Modified Files**

`src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the `<ToastProvider>` children
- Placement ensures proper tracking of all pages in the application

`package.json`:
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` to the dependencies list

`pnpm-lock.yaml`:
- Updated with the new dependency and its transitive dependencies

### Implementation Details

- **Next.js Version**: 16.0.10 (supports App Router)
- **Router Type**: App Router (detected via `app/layout.tsx`)
- **Import Path**: Used `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (correct for Next.js 13.5+)
- **Component Placement**: Added to root layout inside `<body>` tag, ensuring it's included on all pages

### Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Package installed successfully via pnpm
2. ✅ Build completed successfully with no compilation errors
3. ✅ Linter executed - no new errors introduced by this change
4. ✅ Layout.tsx has no linting issues
5. ✅ Lock file (pnpm-lock.yaml) updated properly

### Notes

- The SpeedInsights component will automatically track Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.) when deployed to Vercel
- No configuration needed - the component works out of the box
- Pre-existing linting errors in other files (contact/route.ts, veille/route.ts, Portfolio.tsx, VeilleFeed.tsx) are unrelated to this implementation
- The implementation follows Next.js best practices for App Router with TypeScript
